being with the original ghostbusters was  really like special the new ghostbusters  is here paving a future for the  franchise while using the classics from  the actors all the way to the gadgets  very much worth it it looks so good on  screen the iconic ecto goggles from the  original ghostbusters make an appearance  in the afterlife film as well  they look just incredible but for logan  kim it was very inconvenient since he  couldn't actually see with the goggles  on so when he was acting he literally we  had to like be like look a little left  otherwise he just even know where to  look  luckily the actor made it out totally  unharmed but we can imagine if there's a  sequel he'll be requesting a functional  pair of goggles  it's been a few years since bill murray  sported the classic proton pack and it  wasn't quite like it used to be  murray really suffered feeling a lot of  pain wearing the pack because of how  uncomfortable it was they're pretty  they're very heavy for distant and stunt  shots the actors got to wear a lighter  version of the packs but for any  close-ups it was the real 30 pound deal  like half the weight in what they were  in 1984 the pack was fully equipped with  rumble motors and batteries so those  blasters could jolt and shake in the  actor's hands  driving the ecto-1 was a major throwback  to the original and no doubt a very  special experience for finn wolfhard but  unfortunately the actor didn't get the  chance to fully get behind the wheel he  tried to get his license but  twice i failed wolfhard did get to be in  control of the car as it moved just a  few mere inches but it was still amazing  for the actor a stunt driver took the  reins for the movie controlling the  accelerator and brakes of the totally  souped-up vehicle making this movie was  a multi-year commitment  a year before they even went to camera  the team got into some gardening i was  in the car and it's a real wheat field  that like they planted a year before um  so that we could just rip through it the  house used in the movie was fully real  inside and out and this was where so  many of the scenes were filmed not a  corner was cut here making this movie a  full-time job  ghostbusters afterlife has the best of  both worlds the original cast we know  and love and new actors embodying the  next generation it was amazing it was  really special yeah it didn't really  feel real but it was incredibly special  for the newbies being amid all that  history was definitely something special  it was like a bunch of brothers like  coming back together it was really sweet  this new story has revitalized a  nostalgic franchise brilliantly it's a  fresh take on it all while the new cast  members no doubt felt a ton of pressure  they definitely rose to the challenge a  lot of it is practical step aside cgi  ghostbusters are in town and they like  to keep it retro honoring the original  movies the team relied on good  old-fashioned filming techniques  like puppets and  animatronics wires magnets illusions  if it ain't broke don't fix it a  surprisingly vital tool used throughout  the movie was wind and since they were  kicking at old school the team had a lot  of supplies we had a truck that was only  fan while a major emphasis was put on  practical creations cgi did become key  in bringing one very special and pretty  major element to the movie  one of the most impressive characters we  see in afterlife is the legendary terror  dog and wanting to stay true to the  roots of the film the creature was  brought to life by a mix of practical  and special effects  the only thing cooler than watching it  on screen is actually being on set and  watching the terror dog come to life the  terror dog was a specially built puppet  operated by one of the best puppeteers  in the world this added to the  experience and really made the world of  the movie come to life being the son of  the creator of such a legendary  franchise leaves some pretty big shoes  to fill but luckily jason rickman had  the best right-hand man he could ask for  ivan ritman  such a  family  legacy  his dad was literally right beside him  the whole time giving the director a  very special experience  though sometimes he could feel a bit  overwhelmed by his dad's presence in a  professional setting but at the end of  the day it was a fascinating and  extremely memorable experience as both a  filmmaker and son it is really a gift  that i got to make this movie with him  it wouldn't be ghostbusters without  ghosts but this time we've got muncher  and his casting was totally spontaneous  but it was a perfect match since the  actor just happened to be a major  ghostbusters fan so how did this  serendipitous casting come about josh  and i ran into each other on the sony  lot director jason reitman asked if josh  gad was interested in voicing the ghost  and was delighted when the actor  immediately said yes and went straight  into the studio to record all the  gadgets we see in the film were made to  be as close as possible to the original  ones  as for their references  the real props we were able to get our  hands on the 84 props the team got to  take lidar scans of all those pieces  from the 1984 movie allowing them to  make perfectly accurate replicas to use  we wanted the whole film to be original  recipe ghostbusters the car was put  together with parts found from around  the world mckenna grace even got to wear  the same glasses frames that harold  ramis wore in the original movie i was  just having a great time like just  flying back and forth  while the young actors did have stunt  doubles much of the time the performers  just go straight into their roles um i  got to do some stunts the actress had  never done stunts this intense before  but she bravely dove into wire work and  actually flew across the field protected  of course and landing safely on a  cushiony pad honestly  it really was just like pure excitement  logan kim had quite the unique  experience on set we're not at all  surprised that this was his favorite  scene to film i got to be covered in  marshmallow which was not really  marshmallow as for paul rudd  the whole thing really was fun but boy  going into that store and shooting a  scene  nothing could beat the scene in the mall  featuring the one and only marshmallows  and of course the terror dog he hired a  bagpiper to follow  him  yes  that quote actually has something to do  with the ghostbusters afterlife film  when bill murray's birthday came around  he showed up to set accompanied by an  actual bagpiper but here's the catch the  actor pretended as if the musician  wasn't there at all if that wasn't wild  enough he was singing some  scottish or irish song  to everyone with the bagpiper so how did  the actors deal with this strange  occasion everybody started singing with  him this set was a definite party  and not just for birthdays the now 70  year old actor bill murray was hesitant  about diving back into the franchise he  first starred in decades ago but after  reading the script he knew it was worth  being a part of because of just how much  heart and emotion there was in the story  his concern was fair considering just  how hard the filming wound up being on  him with all the physical action and  wild filming conditions like wind and  dirt this special project has been kept  quite secretive from the very start when  finn wolfhard first auditioned he had no  idea he was reading for none other than  ghostbusters afterlife  it came through as like untitled sony  project since the actor had already  experienced being a ghostbuster in  stranger things he worried he wouldn't  end up getting the role but much to  everyone's delight the job was his  nostalgia a stellar cast and  ghostbusters  we couldn't ask for a more exciting  lineup which special retro gadget would  you want to have
 

